# Jones et al. 2025's rules under WISE broadcast control (arXiv:2305.12773), on the paper's own
# junction grid: our schedules of qccd/repro/sched_wise.py are judged by it.
#
# R4b, R4d and R22 are about a programme's steps and do not apply to a timed schedule; R35-R37
# say the same things of a schedule's moves, with every move's direction read off the machine's
# coordinates rather than taken from its label.

ruleset "jones-wise"
title "Surface-code QCCD under broadcast control"
about "Jones's rules, plus WISE control: one waveform drives every transport move of a cycle, so moves that overlap in time start and end together and make the same motion (primitive and direction, read off the machine's geometry); a trap may sit a cycle out only by its own switch, never do something else; and moves within traps, moves between them and gates never overlap."

include "jones"
use R4d, R4b, R22, R35, R36, R37
